From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:22:39 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 58/72] deepseek: skip index scores whose top-k takes every
 entry (TF_DSV41_IDX_IOTA)

An index layer whose dense top-k reads at most index_topk entries selects
every valid one whatever the scores, so with TF_DSV41_IDX_IOTA=1 its query
projection, rope and score launches are not emitted. The top-k launch stays
with the same arguments, so its selection and counts are byte-identical.
Reindex layers qualify when their candidate source does and the gathered
blocks fit the top-k. The decision is static (config, rows, window end).

Only windows ending at or below 1025 (ratio-2 layers) or 512 (ratio 1 and
reindex) qualify, so at the default TF_DSV41_GRAPH_BUCKET=2048 no graph or
row program changes. Off by default; unset or 0 emits what H emits.

Mechanism after Bertholomus's dsv41 idx_all / iotaVis (round.zig),
re-implemented here; credited in docs/credits.md.

Co-authored-by: bertholomus <311723197+bertholomus@users.noreply.github.com>
